---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Layout title="Privacy" description="What Laissez collects on this site, in the sandbox and in the API, how long it is kept, and what it never does: no third-party trackers, no personal data on-chain, sandbox data deleted after 7 days." path="privacy/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">This page describes exactly what Laissez collects and why, in plain terms. It covers the marketing site, the sandbox and the API. Laissez is pre-launch software run by its founder; there is no data team and no advertising business behind it.</p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 2 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>In one paragraph</h2>
      <p>The site has no cookies, no pixels and no third-party analytics. The sandbox app sends anonymous first-party events to the Laissez API under a random identifier stored in your browser; the API strips anything that looks personal before storing them. Sandboxes contain fictional institutions, people and money and are deleted after 7 days. Tokens that could grant access (sessions, API keys, invites) are stored only as SHA-256 hashes. If you request production access, we keep what you typed into the form and reply by email. Nothing personal is ever written to a blockchain.</p>

      <h2>What is collected, where</h2>
      <table class="grid">
        <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>What</th><th>Why</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>This site</td><td>Nothing. Pages are static files. Fonts load from Google Fonts, which sees your network address like any web request.</td><td>Reading the site</td><td>Not stored by Laissez</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Home page, status page</td><td>Your browser reads public JSON from the API (<code>/v1/status</code>, <code>/v1/metrics/public</code>). No identifier is sent.</td><td>Live figures</td><td>Not stored</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sandbox app</td><td>Anonymous product events (for example <code>sandbox_opened</code>, <code>order_placed</code>) with a random local id kept in your browser's local storage, never linked to a name or email. Property values that look like names, emails, wallets or long numbers are dropped by the API before storage. A hash of your network address is kept for rate limiting only.</td><td>The <a href={url('metrics/')}>live metrics page</a> and improving the product</td><td>Events: 90 days. Hashes: 1 day.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sandbox workspace</td><td>Everything you create in a sandbox: fictional clients, credentials, orders, decisions, settlements, policy changes and the audit log. The sandbox name is the only free text you can give it.</td><td>Running the product</td><td>Deleted with the sandbox 7 days after it is opened</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Account (passkey or SSO)</td><td>Your name, your work email, your passkey's public key and signature counter, your organization's name, your role, and the sessions you have open with device details. No passwords exist.</td><td>Signing you in and showing you your own sessions</td><td>Until you or an administrator removes the account</td></tr>
          <tr><td>API keys, sessions, invites, challenges</td><td>Stored as SHA-256 hashes. The plain value is shown once and never kept.</td><td>Authentication</td><td>Until revoked or expired; expired rows are purged daily</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Request access form</td><td>Name, work email, organization, role, what you distribute, your message, a hash of your network address and your browser's user agent string.</td><td>Replying to you and preventing abuse</td><td>Until the conversation ends or you ask us to delete it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email</td><td>Messages Laissez sends (invites, consent requests, portal links, access request confirmations) are written to an outbox table first. When no email provider is configured they stay there and are shown in the app instead of being sent.</td><td>Delivering the message, and letting sandboxes work without a mail server</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Investor portal and consent pages</td><td>The investor's name as the distributor recorded it, the credential and its classifications, document acknowledgements and subscription requests. Access is by a signed link; the page sends no referrer.</td><td>Showing an investor their own eligibility and documents</td><td>As long as the distributor's organization keeps the client</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Blockchain (testnet)</td><td>Decision outcome, a hash of the inputs and rule-pack versions. Never a name, address, wallet owner or document.</td><td>Proving a decision later without exposing who was checked</td><td>Permanent, by nature of the chain</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>What Laissez does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No third-party trackers, advertising pixels, session recording or fingerprinting, on the site or in the app.</li>
        <li>No cookies. Sign-in state lives in your browser's local storage and is sent only to the Laissez API.</li>
        <li>No selling or sharing of data with anyone for their own purposes.</li>
        <li>No personal data on-chain, in webhooks' signatures, or in product events.</li>
        <li>No real money and no real investors in the sandbox. Every institution and person in it is fictional; thresholds and legal references are real.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who processes the data</h2>
      <p>The API runs on Cloudflare Workers and the database is Neon Postgres, both in a single US region. Email, when a provider is configured, goes through Resend. Fonts come from Google Fonts. Each of these providers sees only what is needed to do its job; none of them receives sandbox content for its own use.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sign out of a sandbox and it is forgotten in your browser immediately; the workspace itself is deleted at the 7-day mark.</li>
        <li>Clear your browser's local storage to reset the anonymous event identifier.</li>
        <li>Ask for your account, organization or access request to be deleted by writing to <a href="mailto:parikshit.ambhore@rice.edu">parikshit.ambhore@rice.edu</a>. Deleting an organization removes its data and keeps only the dated deletion record the audit trail needs.</li>
        <li>Report a security concern to the same address.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this page changes in a way that matters, the date at the top changes with it and the <a href={url('trust/')}>trust page</a> describes the control behind the change. The full text of what the API stores is the code itself.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
